lity":true,"_score_rev_volatility":80.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.09916468275935698,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.02205083157432624,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.1243704100600216,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.11486808340632154,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.03262474264601223,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":41.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.024325967364615054,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":25.7,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02678693550376769,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":40.9,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0008673039940023664,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.81274,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Kronos Worldwide, Inc. produces and markets titanium dioxide pigments (TiO2) in Europe, North America, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. The company offers TiO2 in two crystalline forms comprising rutile and anatase to impart whiteness, brightness, opacity, and durability for various products, including paints, coatings, plastics, paper, fibers, and ceramics, as well as for various specialty products, such as inks, foods, cosmetics, and pharmaceuticals. It also produces and sells ilmenite, a raw material used directly as a feedstock by sulfate-process TiO2 plants; iron-based chemicals, which are used as treatment and conditioning agents for industrial effluents and municipal wastewater, as well as in the manufacture of iron pigments, cement, and agricultural products; and specialty chemicals for use in the formulation of pearlescent pigments, and production of electroceramic capacitors for cell phones and other electronic devices, as well as for use in natural gas pipe and other specialty applications. In addition, the company provides technical services for its products. It sells its products under the KRONOS brand through agents and distributors to paint, plastics, decorative laminate, and paper manufacturers. The company was founded in 1916 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas. Kronos Worldwide, Inc. is a subsidiary of Valhi, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian W. Christian | President, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $822K ranks in the above the sector median among Basic Materials peers. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Kronos Worldwide Inc is a small-cap basic materials business with a $859M market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are contracting by -2.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 21% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $40M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 21.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 81% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 35% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3541801041277482},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.1pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kronos Worldwide (KRO) Q3 Earnings and Revenues Surpass Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025068/kronos-worldwide-kro-q3-earnings-and-revenues-surpass-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3025068","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793923214.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"KRONOS Worldwide Q3 2026 Earnings Preview (NYSE:KRO)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4665356-kronos-worldwide-q3-2026-earnings-preview","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793831999.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Kronos Worldwide (KRO) Projected to Release Earnings on Thursday","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/kronos-worldwide-kro-projected-to-release-earnings-on-thursday.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793721420.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Kronos Worldwide: Q3 Earnings Snapshot","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/kronos-worldwide-q3-earnings-snapshot-223903007.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793918343.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"KRONOS WORLDWIDE, INC. REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2026 RESULTS","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/kronos-worldwide-inc-reports-third-211500754.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793913300.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"ti